## 3. Layer 1 — API / Experience layer (FastAPI)
 
Responsibilities: authentication (Supabase Auth), conversation APIs, streaming, task lifecycle, approvals, recommendations, webhooks, notifications.
 
```
POST /conversations
POST /conversations/{id}/messages          → returns task_id, opens SSE stream
GET  /conversations/{id}/events            → SSE stream (typed events)
 
GET  /tasks/{id}
POST /tasks/{id}/approve                   → resumes checkpointed graph
POST /tasks/{id}/reject
 
GET  /recommendations                      → suggestion cards feed
POST /recommendations/{id}/execute         → creates a gated task
 
POST /webhooks/calendar                    → external event ingestion
```
 
**Rule: FastAPI never executes agent workflows inline.** Every agent invocation is:
 
```
FastAPI → create task row → enqueue (Redis) → worker → LangGraph → persist → notify
```
 
**Typed event stream (required for the chat UX).** Task polling alone is not acceptable for conversation. Workers publish to Redis pub/sub; the gateway relays over SSE/WebSocket as typed events the React Native UI can render as rich components:
 
```json
{ "type": "token",                 "data": "Looking at your carrier..." }
{ "type": "tool_started",          "data": { "tool": "get_current_mobile_plan" } }
{ "type": "recommendation_ready",  "data": { "card": { ... } } }
{ "type": "confirmation_required", "data": { "action_id": "...", "summary": "...", "amount": "£72" } }
{ "type": "action_completed",      "data": { "action_id": "...", "receipt": { ... } } }
{ "type": "error",                 "data": { "code": "...", "retryable": true } }
```
 
