## 7. Agent manifest & registry
 
**Manifest (the plugin descriptor):**
 
```yaml
name: roaming_agent
version: 1.2.0
description: Detects missing roaming coverage and recommends/activates plans
 
triggers:
  events: [trip.detected, trip.updated]
  rules:
    - trip.destination_country != user.home_country
 
required_context:
  - trip.destination_country
  - trip.dates
  - user.home_country
  - user.mobile_provider
  - user.current_plan
  - user.data_usage_preference
 
tools:
  - mobile.get_current_plan          # native adapter
  - mobile.get_roaming_plans         # native adapter
  - mcp.carrier_x.list_addons        # MCP-provided tool (namespaced)
  - web.search                       # native
 
actions:
  - name: activate_roaming_plan
    risk: commit                     # read | draft | commit
    approval: required
    idempotent: true
 
output_schema: RoamingRecommendation
```
 
**Agent Registry** loads manifests at startup, validates them (declared tools exist, declared context keys resolvable, schemas importable), and answers the orchestrator's question *"which capabilities are relevant to this event?"* Adding agent #4 = new folder + manifest. Zero orchestrator changes.
 
Registry table also powers ops: enable/disable an agent per environment, per-user rollout flags, version pinning.
 
