## 18. POC build sequence & acceptance test
 
**Phase 1 — Skeleton (the platform):** FastAPI gateway + auth · task/queue/worker loop · LangGraph supervisor + Postgres checkpointer · Agent & Tool registries (with MCP bridge stub) · typed SSE event stream · Policy Engine with interrupt/approve/resume · core tables + audit · tracing wired.
 
**Phase 2 — Roaming agent end-to-end:** manifest → trigger on `trip.detected` → context resolve → tools (current plan, roaming plans — mock carrier first, real/MCP later) → LLM ranks → recommendation card → user approves → idempotent activation → receipt + audit + memory fact.
 
**Phase 3 — Transit card agent (the architecture test):** web research for destination transit card → `draft` form pre-fill → user submits.
**Acceptance criterion: Phase 3 must not touch orchestration, policy, or gateway code.** If it does, fix the abstraction before agent #3.
 
**Phase 4 — Insurance agent + hardening:** quotes via API/MCP, draft application, commit purchase behind approval + spend limit; load-test workers; eval suites green in CI.
 
